    "poster_id": 171117,
    "post_rendered": "Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a772bd794fbedb2976268c491686644aefc02e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" > and <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/c/d5c12f232787a76f7499dacc975199ddfb05bf02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"15\" >,</span> where <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/7/957fe52a257a56f3d4f7d496b36445f345d5734d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\in \\{1,2, \\dots, 2005 \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"148\" height=\"18\" >,</span> be real numbers such that the inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac4c0e38008d7efdb202b5a728218364aae567c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{i}x-b_{i})^{2} \\ge \\sum_{j=1, j \\not= i}^{2005} (a_{j}x-b_{j})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"231\" height=\"53\" > holds for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/e/c0e43dc938faed17bbd60baac049bf2dd414cb07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" > and all <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/7/957fe52a257a56f3d4f7d496b36445f345d5734d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\in \\{1,2, \\dots, 2005 \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"148\" height=\"18\" >.</span> Find the maximum possible number of positive numbers amongst <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a772bd794fbedb2976268c491686644aefc02e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" > and <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/c/d5c12f232787a76f7499dacc975199ddfb05bf02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"15\" >,</span> <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/7/957fe52a257a56f3d4f7d496b36445f345d5734d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\in \\{1,2, \\dots, 2005 \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"148\" height=\"18\" >.</span>",
    "post_canonical": "Let $a_{i}$ and $b_{i}$, where $i \\in \\{1,2, \\dots, 2005 \\}$, be real numbers such that the inequality $(a_{i}x-b_{i})^{2} \\ge \\sum_{j=1, j \\not= i}^{2005} (a_{j}x-b_{j})$ holds for all $x \\in \\mathbb{R}$ and all $i \\in \\{1,2, \\dots, 2005 \\}$. Find the maximum possible number of positive numbers amongst $a_{i}$ and $b_{i}$, $i \\in \\{1,2, \\dots, 2005 \\}$.",
