    "poster_id": 171117,
    "post_rendered": "Let <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\"  width=\"42\" height=\"13\" >,</span> <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/7/7a707aa1c2f734a9e4767ee9ab57855a8d8cb4e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC \\not= BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"17\" >,</span> be an acute triangle with orthocenter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\"  width=\"16\" height=\"12\" > and incenter <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\"  width=\"9\" height=\"12\" >.</span> The lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/e/20e8e26d580012b86d8fe55e70e5740908c35af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CH$\"  width=\"31\" height=\"12\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/d/a8d37413bae1973358eebff164711f292d16be56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CI$\"  width=\"24\" height=\"12\" > meet the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3df79a4384bc29acd37e14b0430773d09964ddd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup ABC$\"  width=\"58\" height=\"13\" > at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"12\" > and <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\"  width=\"12\" height=\"12\" >,</span> respectively. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7e219a62df6642eb1cbf65825db2ba9887f68e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CIH = 90^{\\circ}$\"  width=\"101\" height=\"13\" > if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/2/0a28d5381d4fde1a5a99ade89c8874e5ef4bbbc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle IDL = 90^{\\circ}$\"  width=\"98\" height=\"13\" >",
    "post_canonical": "Let $ABC$, $AC \\not= BC$, be an acute triangle with orthocenter $H$ and incenter $I$. The lines $CH$ and $CI$ meet the circumcircle of $\\bigtriangleup ABC$ at points $D$ and $L$, respectively. Prove that $\\angle CIH = 90^{\\circ}$ if and only if $\\angle IDL = 90^{\\circ}$",
